.TH REVDEP 1 "2026-09-07" "@PROJECT_NAME@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
revdep \- scan for broken reverse dependencies
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B revdep
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ argument ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B revdep
scans installed binaries, libraries, and language modules for unresolved dependencies. Exclusions are read from \fBrevdep.conf\fR and the files in \fBrevdep.d\fR unless filtering is disabled.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -a, --all
Print all affected files, rather than a summary.
.TP
.B -r, --rebuild
Rebuild and reinstall the package associated with a broken dependency.
.TP
.B -f, --no-filter
Ignore configured excluded directories, files, and libraries.
.TP
.B -e, --exclude PKG...
Exclude packages from a rebuild operation. Use with \fB-r\fR.
.TP
.B -y, --yes
Do not ask for confirmation before rebuilding. Use with \fB-r\fR.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help.
.SH FILES
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/revdep.conf
.br
.I @LIBDIR@/revdep.d/*.conf
.br
.I @SYSCONFDIR@/revdep.d/*.conf
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero when no problem is found or the requested operation succeeds; non-zero when broken dependencies are found or the operation fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR revdep.conf (5),
.BR pkgbuild (1)
